1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:02,020
Let's change seats.

2
00:00:02,230 --> 00:00:06,770
My ordinary high school life
took a turn with this seat change,

3
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:11,839
and turned completely upside down.

4
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:12,540
(I like you.)

5
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:13,670
Huh?

6
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:17,480
Is this some kind of prank?

7
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:21,920
Wait.

8
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,090
If that note...

9
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:25,290
Ah.

10
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,020
Isn't a prank?

11
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:29,779
Teacher Komori?

12
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:33,200
Wait, does that mean I'm getting
in the way of Asamiya's love life?

13
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,730
He's good-looking and smart.

14
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:37,920
He's one of the most
popular guys in school.

15
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:42,340
If I piss off a guy like Asamiya,
my high school life is...

16
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:43,909
What have you been doing this whole time?

17
00:00:43,910 --> 00:00:44,910
Whoa!
It's him.

18
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,670
That note

19
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:48,280
was meant for you, Mayama.

20
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:51,380
Huh?

21
00:00:51,381 --> 00:00:53,020
You're asking what I like about you?

22
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,850
Let's take our time finding out.

23
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:59,219
That helps a lot.

24
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,220
Pointing out my flaws like that.

25
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:02,930
Those aren't your flaws.

26
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,090
Those are the things I
like about you, Mayama.

27
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:08,659
Always putting others first,
even if it means you lose out.

28
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:10,800
That's just how sweet you are, Mayama.

29
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,680
I'm looking forward to getting to know you.

30
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:14,900
After Moving Seats, The Boy Behind
Me Has A Crush On Me (Episode 2)

31
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,040
Asamiya.

32
00:02:35,150 --> 00:02:36,990
When you said you liked me,

33
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:38,390
did you mean...

34
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:48,260
you like me as a friend, right?

35
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,900
Which one do you think it is?

36
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:10,520
Am I dreaming right now?

37
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,100
(How you tend to slouch.) (How you always have bedhead.)
(How you always take the short end of the stick.)

38
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:35,340
Those are the things I
like about you, Mayama.

39
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:44,090
Since that day, Asamiya's sticky note
attacks have only gotten more intense.

40
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:49,520
At this rate, before the
first semester is even over,

41
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:53,060
my entire notebook will
be covered in sticky notes.

42
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:06,069
Did something good happen?

43
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:06,760
Huh?

44
00:04:06,761 --> 00:04:08,420
It's just rare,

45
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,040
for you to be up this early, Hare.

46
00:04:11,410 --> 00:04:13,450
I do this sometimes.

47
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:15,780
I'm heading out now.

48
00:04:16,950 --> 00:04:17,950
Ah, wait.

49
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:20,090
You've got a cowlick.

50
00:04:20,091 --> 00:04:23,560
Ah, this... It's fine like this.

51
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:25,130
Huh?

52
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:26,730
I'm off!

53
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:48,320
Morning.

54
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,480
Ah...

55
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,920
Morning.

56
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:56,330
You really left your hair sticking up.

57
00:04:56,930 --> 00:05:00,100
You said you wanted to
touch it every three days, right?

58
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,970
I'd touch it every day if I could.

59
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,000
What's that?

60
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:10,470
A thank-you for last time.

61
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:13,610
Bread?

62
00:05:13,710 --> 00:05:17,010
Didn't you buy me bread
at the cafeteria before?

63
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:19,650
So I bought some at the convenience store.

64
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:25,720
Asamiya?

65
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:32,600
When I die, please put this
in my coffin with me.

66
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,700
Don't do that. Eat it now
before it goes bad.

67
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:39,130
Got it.

68
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:40,420
Thanks.

69
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:41,540
Yeah.

70
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,580
Also,

71
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:52,740
writing all those sticky notes must
be tiring. You can slow down, it's fine.

72
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,580
I thought I was already holding back a lot.

73
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,890
Huh?

74
00:05:57,050 --> 00:05:58,850
Because I've barely written anything yet.

75
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:04,960
But since you mentioned it,
I'll keep it in mind.

76
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:07,700
Thanks.

77
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,800
Asamiya is really sweet.

78
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:16,540
I enjoy spending time with him, too.

79
00:06:17,670 --> 00:06:18,670
But...

80
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:23,579
At the time, I had no idea that
becoming friends with Asamiya

81
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:27,809
would lead to another problem.

82
00:06:27,810 --> 00:06:30,120
Morning!

83
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:33,790
Asamiya walking to school with someone?
That's a rare sight.

84
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:34,890
Right?

85
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:40,000
Becoming friends with Asamiya

86
00:06:41,530 --> 00:06:45,470
meant I also had to deal with
these popular guys.

87
00:06:45,970 --> 00:06:47,209
Did you do the homework?

88
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:49,240
- Nope.
- You look like you didn't.

89
00:06:49,850 --> 00:06:51,090
I knew you definitely wouldn't.

90
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,890
Sakaki, did you break up again?

91
00:07:03,350 --> 00:07:04,890
We just weren't a good match.

92
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:06,230
Wait a minute.

93
00:07:06,910 --> 00:07:09,190
What's your longest relationship so far?

94
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,730
Huh? But...

95
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:14,960
Hmm... One, two, three...?

96
00:07:15,670 --> 00:07:16,670
Two... three months?

97
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,000
More like two or three weeks.

98
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,200
Bingo.

99
00:07:19,201 --> 00:07:21,200
It's like a conversation
from another world.

100
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:22,800
What about you, Asamiya?

101
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:24,750
Is there anyone you're
interested in right now?

102
00:07:25,610 --> 00:07:27,150
Maybe.

103
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,010
Huh? Really?

104
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:29,850
Who is it?
Who?

105
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:31,930
I can't believe Asamiya has someone.

106
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:32,950
That's rare.

107
00:07:33,350 --> 00:07:34,520
Alright, enough about me.

108
00:07:35,090 --> 00:07:37,620
What about you, Sakaki? Got
your eye on someone new?

109
00:07:38,410 --> 00:07:41,960
Hmm... Not this time, actually.

110
00:07:42,970 --> 00:07:43,970
Ah.

111
00:07:44,090 --> 00:07:45,430
Maybe I should consider Mayama.

112
00:07:46,150 --> 00:07:47,150
Huh?

113
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:50,500
It's fine, I have a wide strike zone.
I'm totally down.

114
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:52,170
No, that's...

115
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:55,500
Sorry.
You should find someone else.

116
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:56,640
Huh?

117
00:07:56,910 --> 00:07:59,340
Nah, I was totally joking.

118
00:07:59,410 --> 00:08:00,410
Makes sense.

119
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:05,380
If your strike zone is that wide,
who else is there besides Mayama?

120
00:08:20,530 --> 00:08:21,560
What's wrong?

121
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:22,770
Nothing.

122
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,940
Do you work out, Asamiya?

123
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:29,250
No.

124
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:31,210
I just sprint to the station sometimes.

125
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:32,940
That's impressive.

126
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,840
Look at me, I'm just skin and bones.

127
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:39,590
I like you no matter how you look.

128
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:41,420
No, that's not it.

129
00:08:43,170 --> 00:08:44,170
Wait.

130
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,470
Can you put your jacket on?

131
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,160
Huh?

132
00:08:51,530 --> 00:08:53,610
But we're doing endurance
running today. I'll sweat.

133
00:08:53,830 --> 00:08:54,900
Exactly.

134
00:08:57,150 --> 00:08:59,940
Last time, your shirt
got a bit see-through.

135
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,410
But I didn't bring my track jacket today...

136
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:10,010
You can wear mine.

137
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:12,980
I can't let anyone else see.

138
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,820
Who would be happy
seeing my bare skin anyway?

139
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:19,850
I would.

140
00:09:22,090 --> 00:09:23,190
I'll go on ahead.

141
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,540
Ah...

142
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:44,350
It smells like Asamiya.

143
00:09:46,450 --> 00:09:48,850
What the hell am I thinking?

144
00:09:50,930 --> 00:09:53,590
One, two, three, four.

145
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:57,160
Five, six, seven.

146
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:03,570
Maybe when Asamiya says he likes me,

147
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:08,300
it's just the kind of casual 'like'
popular guys throw around all the time.

148
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:12,110
Sakaki gave off the same vibe earlier.

149
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:17,080
Alright,
pair up and do some stretches.

150
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:23,320
Uh...

151
00:10:31,290 --> 00:10:33,400
Mayama, are you flexible?

152
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:34,630
No.

153
00:10:34,631 --> 00:10:36,430
I'm stiff. Super stiff.

154
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,830
Then I'll go easy on you.

155
00:10:39,370 --> 00:10:40,370
Thanks.

156
00:10:44,950 --> 00:10:46,580
Ow, ow, ow, ow! That hurts!

157
00:10:46,590 --> 00:10:48,290
Were you lying just now?

158
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:51,730
Wait... I tap out, I tap out!

159
00:10:52,310 --> 00:10:53,350
No tapping out.

160
00:10:55,130 --> 00:10:57,020
I can't, I'm gonna split in half!

161
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:58,870
I'm seriously gonna split!

162
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:00,849
Wanna try pushing past your limits?

163
00:11:00,850 --> 00:11:02,390
Ah... Wait!

164
00:11:02,890 --> 00:11:04,460
Ow, wait a sec!

165
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:05,759
It hurts!

166
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,000
Switch.

167
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,200
What a shame.

168
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:23,550
Alright, I'm gonna push.

169
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:24,850
Yeah.

170
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:30,470
Is this the 'I'm not gonna cooperate' mode?

171
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:31,910
I'm already using all my strength.

172
00:11:35,090 --> 00:11:36,990
Have you ever heard of karma?

173
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:39,010
Huh?

174
00:11:40,710 --> 00:11:42,030
Wait, time out!

175
00:11:42,830 --> 00:11:43,600
Seriously, stop for a sec!

176
00:11:43,601 --> 00:11:46,470
You tortured me just now.
This is nothing.

177
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:54,440
Ah, sorry.

178
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:06,610
Huh?

179
00:12:07,270 --> 00:12:08,270
Hey.

180
00:12:08,330 --> 00:12:10,050
What are you two flirting about over there?

181
00:12:12,730 --> 00:12:14,030
We got interrupted.

182
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,650
Shouldn't you take this run seriously?

183
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,300
I am running.

184
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:36,420
That's not what I meant.

185
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,440
Asamiya.

186
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,460
You can definitely run faster than this.

187
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,060
See?

188
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,460
Wait for me.

189
00:12:45,461 --> 00:12:46,800
I'll lap you and come find you.

190
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,960
Hey, Mayama.

191
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:02,300
Have you and Asamiya
suddenly gotten super close lately?

192
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:03,650
Have we?

193
00:13:03,651 --> 00:13:07,650
Because lately, Asamiya spends
more time with you than with us.

194
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:12,820
Honestly,
what do you think of Asamiya?

195
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:14,720
What do you mean?

196
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,300
I don't know.

197
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:25,030
He's just too far out of reach.

198
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:29,040
Out of reach, huh.

199
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:47,660
It's so hot.

200
00:13:47,690 --> 00:13:49,220
Mayama, come here for a sec.

201
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,836
Asamiya said he has something to tell you.

202
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:52,860
Huh?

203
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,740
Sorry to keep you waiting.

204
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:02,280
Yeah...

205
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,920
I'm sorry.

206
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,980
I did something to upset you, didn't I?

207
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,400
You were mad just now, right?

208
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,550
I was.

209
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,020
Yeah, I was.

210
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,600
Even though I told you to wait for me...

211
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:18,120
Huh?

212
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:20,660
You ran off with Sakaki and the others.

213
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,620
Be more mindful next time.

214
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,960
Okay.

215
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:27,380
Um... okay?

216
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,019
Is this what you wanted
to talk to me about?

217
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:32,980
Wait, didn't you say
you wanted to talk to me?

218
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,000
Huh?

219
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,140
Oh crap, we're busted.

220
00:14:36,770 --> 00:14:38,039
Ah, wait...

221
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,040
We'll leave you two alone.

222
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:43,819
If you feel like Asamiya is out of your league,
then just try harder to get closer to him.

223
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:44,850
What should we do?

224
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:45,986
They'll probably get bored of this soon.

225
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,550
You're way too calm about this.

226
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:49,640
Whoa.

227
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:54,090
Were you talking about
me being out of your league?

228
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:59,130
Well, how should I put this...

229
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,320
What's wrong?

230
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,879
I was sweating, and then the wind blew...

231
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,210
Mayama looks cold, Asamiya.

232
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,710
Warm him up.

233
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,880
It's fine. I'm used to this kind of thing.

234
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:26,420
Huh?

235
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:35,080
If we don't do this,
they'll never stop, right?

236
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,040
Do I still feel out of your league now?

237
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:53,150
You smell like Mayama.

238
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,590
People will get the wrong idea.

239
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:57,960
The wrong idea?

240
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,680
I mean...

241
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:02,320
You said you like me.

242
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,860
When you said you like me,
you meant as a friend, right?

243
00:16:07,030 --> 00:16:09,200
You probably say that
to everyone else, too.

244
00:16:11,370 --> 00:16:12,500
As if I would.

245
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:14,959
Alright, that's enough.

246
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,729
PDA time is over.

247
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:17,410
Did you get the shot?
Got it perfectly.

248
00:16:18,321 --> 00:16:20,361
This is definitely getting
over ten thousand likes.

249
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:24,580
I'll kill you if you post that.

250
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,420
Just kidding.

251
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,020
We wouldn't actually do that.

252
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:36,590
I kinda want to post it, though.

253
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:37,860
I guess that's a no-go?

254
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,300
Our follower count would skyrocket.

255
00:16:39,930 --> 00:16:41,060
Asamiya?

256
00:16:41,730 --> 00:16:44,330
I'm sending it to my
phone before I delete it.

257
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,240
Why?

258
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:50,470
If you don't like it,
I'll delete it right away.

259
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:54,010
If you're just keeping it
for yourself, I guess it's fine.

260
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:55,340
Then I'll treat it as a family heirloom.

261
00:16:55,341 --> 00:16:57,650
No, please don't.

262
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:13,900
Mayama.

263
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:15,930
Come here for a sec.

264
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:18,280
Huh?

265
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,100
Is this...

266
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:24,440
Am I about to get beaten up?

267
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:30,350
Because I got too close to Asamiya?

268
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,320
Listen.

269
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,600
We're sorry.

270
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,520
Huh?

271
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:49,000
Asamiya chewed us out after that.

272
00:17:49,330 --> 00:17:50,800
He said we took the joke too far.

273
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:51,740
You see,

274
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:52,870
Asamiya,

275
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:55,000
he barely talks to anyone
other than us.

276
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:58,070
But he's opened up to you.

277
00:17:59,270 --> 00:18:01,640
So we were really happy about it, too.

278
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:03,980
And we just got totally carried away.

279
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,250
We're sorry.

280
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:07,480
You don't have to apologize like that.

281
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:10,250
We want to be good friends with you, too.

282
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:11,550
Huh?

283
00:18:11,551 --> 00:18:13,160
Don't just hang out with Asamiya.

284
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:14,860
Hang out with us, too.

285
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,230
No, someone like me...

286
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,160
Never mind.

287
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:27,860
Let's get along from now on.

288
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,940
Let's get along.

289
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:32,780
That's great.

290
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,180
Maybe we're the same.

291
00:18:36,910 --> 00:18:40,050
Even though I arbitrarily labeled them
as the popular kids,

292
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:42,850
after talking to them like this,

293
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:48,360
I realized Sakaki and Tsunekawa
are just normal classmates.

294
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:50,500
I'm sure...

295
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:53,030
Do I still feel out of your league now?

296
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,400
I'm sure Asamiya is, too...

297
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:02,700
Asamiya.

298
00:19:04,410 --> 00:19:06,610
You're hanging out with
those two behind my back again.

299
00:19:06,910 --> 00:19:08,580
No, you've got it wrong.

300
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,240
This is...

301
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:14,850
Because we're friends.

302
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,050
Sakaki and Tsunekawa, too.

303
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,720
So isn't it normal for us all to get along?

304
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:25,090
I don't like being told
who I can be friends with.

305
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:29,380
I'm sorry.

306
00:19:31,430 --> 00:19:33,200
Alright, I have a proposal.

307
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:36,216
It's about time to start prepping
for the cultural festival, right?

308
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:38,910
Mayama, you should be on
the planning committee with us.

309
00:19:39,370 --> 00:19:40,619
The planning committee?

310
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:42,240
That's a great idea.

311
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,240
What do you say?
Asamiya, just the four of us.

312
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:47,880
Sounds good to me.

313
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,379
Awesome, then it's settled.

314
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:50,679
Great, let's go.

315
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,379
- Let's go.
- The planning committee, huh.

316
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,579
What does the planning committee do?

317
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:55,579
Whatever we want.
Like a maid cafe or something.

318
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:57,039
A maid cafe?

319
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,560
A maid cafe sounds good,
right? Everyone in maid outfits.

320
00:19:58,584 --> 00:19:59,836
Asamiya in a maid outfit
would be a rare sight.

321
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:01,240
- I kinda want to see that.
- Hey.

322
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:02,396
- Then it's decided, maid outfits it is.
- It'd look cool.

323
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:04,930
- Everyone wants to see it.
- Any other ideas?

324
00:20:09,870 --> 00:20:11,240
You don't hate it, do you?

325
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:13,380
Huh?

326
00:20:14,210 --> 00:20:16,210
Being on the cultural
festival planning committee.

327
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:18,250
We didn't force you into it, did we?

328
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:21,220
It's fine.

329
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:26,420
You're always so worried
about that, Asamiya.

330
00:20:28,190 --> 00:20:30,560
Always worrying if I hate something.

331
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:35,600
I'd rather die than do something you hate.

332
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:38,820
About hugging you on the balcony earlier...

333
00:20:39,970 --> 00:20:41,740
If you hated it, I want to apologize.

334
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:53,020
I think it's really sweet of you.

335
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:57,450
I'm going this way.

336
00:20:58,640 --> 00:20:59,640
See you tomorrow.

337
00:21:03,530 --> 00:21:05,430
When Asamiya said he likes me,

338
00:21:06,330 --> 00:21:09,060
he didn't mean it as a friend...

339
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:35,060
Does that mean I'll have to
give him a proper answer someday?

340
00:21:37,390 --> 00:21:39,830
I don't dislike Asamiya.

341
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:44,270
Knowing he likes me actually makes me...

342
00:21:45,330 --> 00:21:46,340
feel really happy.

343
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:50,070
But...

344
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:58,180
If I really had to give an answer,

345
00:21:59,350 --> 00:22:00,980
that answer wouldn't be yes.

346
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:05,720
I'm really happy about your feelings.

347
00:22:05,790 --> 00:22:06,790
But...

348
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:09,320
I'm sorry.

349
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:11,760
What are you talking about?

350
00:22:11,890 --> 00:22:12,890
Huh?

351
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:17,060
Hey, hey.
Of course it was a joke.

352
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:19,800
As if anyone would actually like Mayama.

353
00:22:19,820 --> 00:22:20,820
Yeah, right.

354
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,919
- He actually took it seriously.
- Are you for real?

355
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:25,919
Why would someone that cute
ever like you?

356
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:27,880
Stop flattering yourself.

357
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,280
Someone like me

358
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:39,350
is completely out of Asamiya's league.

359
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:47,400
Asamiya is probably just
having a momentary lapse in judgment.

360
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:15,750
(Next Episode Preview) Our class activity
for the cultural festival is a haunted house.

361
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:19,499
Could it be that you have someone you like?

362
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:22,199
We decided to have
Mayama play the werewolf.

363
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,200
So cute.

364
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,290
All done.

365
00:24:25,820 --> 00:24:26,860
Did I scare you?

366
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:30,570
Why do I like him so much?

367
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,040
The only thing I know for sure is,

368
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:36,440
Mayama is my first love.

369
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:38,540
You're way too hard on yourself.

370
00:24:38,860 --> 00:24:39,860
Mayama.

371
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:41,180
Here you go.

372
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:42,010
Huh?

373
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:43,539
It goes perfectly with the name Hare.

374
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:45,040
This is also a return gift.

375
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:49,360
Being told by Asamiya that he likes me...
I think I'm actually pretty happy about it.

376
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:53,079
Asamiya could definitely
find someone better.

377
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:56,690
I fell for you
because you're Mayama.
